issues.body:
### Minecraft Version

26.1.2

### What happened?

# Description
When the client first launches and loads a world for the first time, curios items already equipped by the player will not apply their attribute modifiers. If the item is then unequipped and re-equipped, the attribute modifiers will be applied correctly. This issue does not occur when the world is simply reloaded; it requires a full client restart.

# How to reproduce
## In mod dev
1. register a new curios slot type "my_slot" via datagen
2. register a new item "my_heart" available for this slot, with curios attribute modifier that adds 20 max health
3. launch the game, create a new level, equip "my_heart" in "my_slot", and change to survival mode
4. normally, you can see 2 rows of red hearts or heart containers on the hud
5. close the level and shut down the whole client
6. restart the game, and open the level before

## Expected
you can see 2 rows of red hearts or heart containers on the hud

## Actual
you can only see 1 row of red hearts

# Simple Analyze
In ```top.theillusivec4.curios.api.CuriosSlotTypes#getSlotTypes()```, ```FMLLoader.getCurrent().getDist().isClient()``` will return ```CLIENT``` although it's running in server thread in singleplayer. 
```
  public static Map<String, ISlotType> getSlotTypes() {
    return getSlotTypes(FMLLoader.getCurrent().getDist().isClient());
  }
```
When the client just launched and a world just loaded, ```top.theillusivec4.curios.common.data.CuriosSlotResources#CLIENT``` is not sync with server's, which follows: 
```
at top.theillusivec4.curios.api.CuriosSlotTypes.getSlotTypes(CuriosSlotTypes.java:25)
at top.theillusivec4.curios.api.type.ISlotType.get(ISlotType.java:58)
at top.theillusivec4.curios.api.common.slot.SlotTypePredicate.matches(SlotTypePredicate.java:97)
at top.theillusivec4.curios.api.CurioAttributeModifiers.forEach(CurioAttributeModifiers.java:115)
at top.theillusivec4.curios.api.type.capability.ICurioItem.forEachModifier(ICurioItem.java:70)
at top.theillusivec4.curios.common.CuriosCommonEvents.lambda$tick$0(CuriosCommonEvents.java:555)

```
and cause ```top.theillusivec4.curios.api.common.slot.SlotTypePredicate#matches(java.lang.String)``` here slotType == null
```
  public boolean matches(String slotId) {
    ISlotType slotType = ISlotType.get(slotId);
    return slotType != null && this.matches(slotType);
  }
```
and at line 555 of ```top.theillusivec4.curios.common.CuriosCommonEvents#tick``` that ```action``` in ```forEachModifier``` will not action and finally akip adding attribute modifiers
```
 if (!stack.isEmpty()) {
                    ICurioItem
                        .forEachModifier(stack, slotContext,
                            (attributeHolder, attributeModifier) -> {
                              if (attributeHolder.value() instanceof SlotAttribute slotAttribute) {
                                handler.addTransientSlotModifier(
                                    slotAttribute.id(),
                                    attributeModifier.id(), attributeModifier.amount(),
                                    attributeModifier.operation());
                              } else {
                                AttributeInstance instance =
                                    attributeMap.getInstance(attributeHolder);

                                if (instance != null) {
                                  instance.addOrUpdateTransientModifier(
                                      attributeModifier);
                                }
                              }
                            });
```

### Relevant Log Outputs

_No response_

### Minecraft Version

26.1 (had to edit this in, because 1.21.11 is the highest the drop-down goes)

### What happened?

btw, this template needs 26.1 added to it.

This happened in Neoforge 26.1-26.1.0.19 for curios-neoforge-15.0.0-beta.1+26.1

The toolbelt is in the belt slot, and I activate it to insert a tool that happens to be enchanted and the server crashes each time I do it. I had to nbt edit the belt out of character data to fix the crash.

I first posted this to gigaherz's issue tracker whereby I was directed to post it here. 

https://github.com/gigaherz/ToolBelt/issues/172#issuecomment-4217968873

